  "_traversal": "drift and nb are the SECOND AXIS of behaviour, and the first that comes from analysing the corpus rather than from naming a category. The 22 machines differ in rhythm and envelope; none of them differed in how it moves through the material, because until descriptors existed there was no geometry to move through. Sustained machines hold the target nearly still in a narrow neighbourhood; machinic ones roam widely. Both are data, so a new traversal can be invented without writing a pattern.",
  "_layers": "Each machine's MEASURED median event duration, and the grain layer that fits it. Taken from dump_events.scd, not assigned by hand. The vocabulary spans 0.013 s (ma, cr) to 11.4 s (bu), nearly a thousandfold, so no single grain length can serve it: at 0.5 s the fast machines smeared five grains into every event, at 0.06 s the slow ones became isolated clicks separated by silence. micro = 60 ms onset-aligned grains, macro = 2 s. Runtime machines with no entry default to micro."
